-- OSDU Well / Wellbore prototype: Spark SQL + Apache Iceberg
-- Scope: "OSDU Well-Wellbore Prototype Entities.xlsx", Entities and Reference Data.
-- 18 scenario entities + 47 reference-data types = 65 record tables.
-- Columns: latest semver in Generated/ for each workbook kind; exact versions
-- and source SHA-256 digests are recorded per table below.
-- DDL reference: https://iceberg.apache.org/docs/latest/spark-ddl/
--
-- PREREQUISITES
-- Install the Iceberg Spark runtime matching your Spark/Scala versions and
-- configure an Iceberg catalog called osdu_iceberg before starting spark-sql.
-- For example, a Hadoop catalog requires these Spark configuration keys:
--   spark.sql.catalog.osdu_iceberg=org.apache.iceberg.spark.SparkCatalog
--   spark.sql.catalog.osdu_iceberg.type=hadoop
--   spark.sql.catalog.osdu_iceberg.warehouse=<your-warehouse-URI>
-- Use your own REST/Hive/Glue catalog configuration instead when appropriate.
-- Replace `osdu_iceberg` throughout this file if your catalog has another name.
-- The configured warehouse supplies managed table locations; none are hardcoded.
-- Execute: spark-sql [your catalog/runtime configuration] -f this-file.sql
--
-- REPRESENTATION / LOADING CONTRACT
-- One row is an OSDU record version. Keep id and version as supplied by OSDU.
-- Envelope fields are columns; data remains a typed STRUCT. Arrays remain
-- ARRAYs, compositions remain STRUCTs, and record references remain STRING IDs
-- (including any trailing version segment), never surrogate integer keys.
-- allOf fragments are merged; object oneOf alternatives become nullable field
-- supersets. JSON Schema exclusivity, patterns, enums, nested required fields,
-- units and record-kind compatibility must be validated before ingestion.
-- Root NOT NULL follows source required lists only; id is not made mandatory
-- where the source schema does not require it. Uniqueness of (id, version) and
-- referential integrity are loader responsibilities, not Iceberg constraints.
-- JSON integers -> BIGINT, numbers -> DOUBLE, date-time -> UTC TIMESTAMP,
-- date -> DATE. Parse timestamps and check range/precision before loading.
-- Known arbitrary objects -> MAP<STRING, STRING>, with EVERY map value encoded
-- as JSON text (including quotes around JSON string values). Incompatible union
-- values (e.g. GeoJSON coordinate arrays of different ranks) -> STRING holding
-- the JSON text of that entire value. See per-table exception paths below.
-- tags is a normal MAP<STRING, STRING>; its values are plain strings, not JSON.
-- _raw_record is an added, optional STRING for the complete original record JSON.
-- Populate it to preserve undeclared extensions and source lexical precision.
-- Never load JSON objects/arrays into fallback STRING fields by an implicit cast:
-- explicitly serialize them to JSON before applying the typed table projection.
-- ACL/legal fields store metadata; they do not enforce access or legal policy.
-- Reference-data tables are empty definitions; no reference values are seeded.
-- The workbook is not transitively closed: references to other OSDU kinds remain
-- valid IDs, but this script creates only the 65 requested tables.
-- File.Generic and FileCollection.Generic use underscores in SQL table names.
-- Iceberg v2 / Parquet, initially unpartitioned; no PK/FK/index/identity syntax.
-- IF NOT EXISTS permits reruns but does NOT migrate an existing table's schema.

SET spark.sql.session.timeZone = UTC;

CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS `osdu_iceberg`.`master_data`;

CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS `osdu_iceberg`.`work_product_component`;

CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS `osdu_iceberg`.`work_product`;

CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS `osdu_iceberg`.`dataset`;

CREATE NAMESPACE IF NOT EXISTS `osdu_iceberg`.`reference_data`;

